# The oracle's pinned revision: the
# 9.2.0 release (tag `mockserver-9.2.0`; 9.1.0 before), whose parent's Buildkite build passed
# and whose release commit changes only versions, and the images its release tags name, pinned by the digests those
# tags resolve to (`9.2.0`, `clustered-9.2.0`, `9.2.0-http3`, `mockserver-webhook:9.2.0`). Release images carry an
# empty revision label (the webhook none), so the pairing is shown by running the arm64 image: `version: 9.2.0` and
# `mock_server_build_info{git_hash="789142c1"}`. Read by the Makefile (`include`), shell scripts (`.`)
# and the Rust tests (`include_str!`). Re-pin: all values together, and `upstream/mockserver` and `spec/mockserver`
# moved to the same commit.
ORACLE_REVISION=789142c14c8a20c3483603b48d7e5b849d918317
ORACLE_VERSION=9.2.0
ORACLE_IMAGE=mockserver/mockserver@sha256:016f7d16bc88d2e1aa52d5a177f1aafee758cf70bea5e0624b0ab2c32f394df1
ORACLE_CLUSTERED_IMAGE=mockserver/mockserver@sha256:4bf0abd22148abad538eb4de4310a6d31073d7712f52739ebf9352d8d36afec5
ORACLE_HTTP3_IMAGE=mockserver/mockserver@sha256:ff4b231bd16168ce59e0430c8cdbeb8fd9ab6f75fc0c0369285a9d27e111fca6
ORACLE_WEBHOOK_IMAGE=mockserver/mockserver-webhook@sha256:7b5c13803335cb45fb3fe924ca6252c31fc0b81ad42db6b6da492b1432fd31bc
# The machine the oracle sizes itself for: `actionHandlerThreadCount` defaults to max(5, the JVM's
# processors) and `maxEventLogSizeInBytes`, `maxOpenAiResponsesSizeInBytes`, ... to fractions of its heap ceiling,
# so every oracle container recording starts gets `JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS=-XX:ActiveProcessorCount=<cpus> -Xmx<heap>`
# and reports the same values on any VM. The values are those of the 6-CPU, 32 GiB (33587785728 bytes) container VM the
# 9.1.0 goldens were recorded on: the image's `-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=45.0` of that memory, ZGC-aligned up to 2 MiB.
# Our side's test constants (`ORACLE_ACTIVE_PROCESSORS`, `ORACLE_CONTAINER_MEMORY_BYTES` in src/config.rs) must agree.
ORACLE_ACTIVE_PROCESSORS=6
ORACLE_MAX_HEAP_BYTES=15116271616
